Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: wlcore/wl12xx: boot debug for the chip id and top register status

On the N8 the probe stops at "Top register access timed out" with
nothing about what came before. With DEBUG_BOOT (wlcore.debug_level bit
2) print the chip id that wl12xx_get_hw_info read and the last OCP data
word of a timed out top register read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ti/wl12xx/main.c | 1 +
 drivers/net/wireless/ti/wlcore/main.c | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ti/wlcore/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ti/wlcore/main.c
@@ -6125,6 +6125,7 @@
 	ret = wlcore_read_reg(wl, REG_CHIP_ID_B, &wl->chip.id);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto out;
+	wl1271_debug(DEBUG_BOOT, "hw info: chip id 0x%x", wl->chip.id);
 
 	wl->fuse_oui_addr = 0;
 	wl->fuse_nic_addr = 0;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ti/wl12xx/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ti/wl12xx/main.c
@@ -766,6 +766,7 @@
 	} while (!(val & OCP_READY_MASK) && --timeout);
 
 	if (!timeout) {
+		wl1271_debug(DEBUG_BOOT, "top reg (ocp addr 0x%x): ocp data 0x%x", addr, val);
 		wl1271_warning("Top register access timed out.");
 		return -ETIMEDOUT;
 	}
